00:19:10.590 --> 00:19:16.960
the fourth state of matter, that is heated
gas.

00:19:16.960 --> 00:19:22.030
Luffy tells us that he cant let the gas escape
his body or it's over. So luffy literally

00:19:22.030 --> 00:19:27.310
seeming to melt, might be him heating up and
creating plasma inside his rubber body, using

00:19:27.310 --> 00:19:34.300
the power of the sun itself to unleash incredible
forces. As binks sake said, the morning sun

00:19:34.300 --> 00:19:36.940
will rise.

00:19:36.940 --> 00:19:42.121
And while I like this idea a lot, it doesn't
explain the cartoony part of his powers. What's

00:19:42.121 --> 00:19:48.190
the deal with that? Well, basically since
day 1 Luffy's fighting style has always been

00:19:48.190 --> 00:19:52.830
cartoonish but he had limitations (like when
he tried the spinny spinny attack on Arlong

00:19:52.830 --> 00:19:56.270
and got stuck and almost died in the process).

00:19:56.270 --> 00:20:02.820
Similar to Yu-Gi-Oh, toon powers are incredible
because they can go against the laws of time,

00:20:02.820 --> 00:20:09.120
space, gravity, and so on. It truly seems
to allow Luffy to Fight in any way he pleases.

00:20:09.120 --> 00:20:15.120
Like expanding his limbs, changing the world
around him and ignoring how physics work.

00:20:15.120 --> 00:20:19.770
As the Gorosei explain: Making people laugh
wherever it goes, It's the most ridiculous

00:20:19.770 --> 00:20:25.960
power in the world. Maybe quite literally
as Luffy can turn things into a funny cartoon.

00:20:25.960 --> 00:20:30.560
Which would be the most Oda-like thing to
do.

00:20:30.560 --> 00:20:35.440
But knowing this by itself isn't enough yet,
we will need to see Luffy's fight with Kaido

00:20:35.440 --> 00:20:40.180
play out in full to really understand Luffy's
true powers.

00:20:40.180 --> 00:20:44.520
And that's why you really shouldn't skip this
video here, where I explain in detail how

00:20:44.520 --> 00:20:50.370
Kaido tried to awaken this power himself and
what it means for the end of this fight.

